  "G14 hard guard: workflow word 'admitted' at handbook/parts/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:681 ('cross-sort equality is admitted'); lint wording, not a coverage gap.",
  "handbook/annex/p02/higher-order-supplement.tex:22-60 (annex:p2.hol.5) proves thm:p02-many-sorted-translation only at summary level ('Induction on terms, then on well-sorted formulas, gives ...'); the case-by-case proof is written in handbook/annex/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:107-205, 207-345, 347-395, so no coverage gap results.",
  "handbook/parts/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:614-616 cites Pitts1995Draft Example 2.3.2 p. 11 for the rule 'remove a variable from a context only when its sort is inhabited by the signature'; printed p. 11 shows only the hegel example (T=F:bool [x:hegel] a theorem, T=F:bool [] not), i.e. the phenomenon, not that rule formulation. Source-fidelity observation; the citation is supporting, not an owed component. The first citation at handbook/parts/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:530-531 matches the page.",
  "handbook/annex/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:93-103: the letter t names a sort chosen outside S_0 and is then reused at lines 102-103 for 'some sort t' obtained from the property of T; notational clash (the argument stands because Sigma contains every not-Q_s(e)).",
  "handbook/parts/p02/variants.tex:35-40 restricts Sort, F, R to at most countable ('Larger signatures ... are not in the scope of that theorem'); the owned variants inherit it and empty-sort clause 4 (handbook/parts/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:592-596; handbook/annex/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:551-561) uses it. Announced boundary.",
  "handbook/parts/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02-p02-038.tex:681-684 announces that order-sorted signatures (declared sort inclusions) and overloaded symbols are not treated."
